Subject: [PATCH] PWHM HAL fix for Wireless Backhaul Switching

Addressed multiple issues in wireless backhaul switching functionality for
PWHM HAL implementation:

1. Backhaul Manager improvements:
   - Fixed code indentation and formatting
   - Updated log messages to reference 'bpl_cfg' instead of 'UCI config'
   - Added error handling to continue on credential retrieval failure
   - Improved credential validation logic for wireless backhaul switching

2. STA WLAN HAL enhancements:
   - Refactored disconnect logic to use set_profile_enable(false) instead
     of remove_profile() for cleaner profile management
   - Enhanced disconnect_backhaul_sta() with proper status updates
   - Improved reconnect_backhaul_sta() to enable both profile and endpoint
   - Fixed code formatting and added better error handling
   - Added status update calls before critical operations

3. BPL WiFi configuration support:
   - Extended bpl_cfg_get_wifi_security_object() to support both AP and
     STA (EndPoint) interfaces
   - Added logic to search for enabled Profile in EndPoint when interface
     is not found as AP
   - Enables proper credential retrieval for STA interfaces during
     backhaul switching scenarios

These changes ensure reliable wireless backhaul switching by properly
managing profile states and retrieving credentials from the correct
configuration sources for both AP and STA interfaces.

Signed-off-by: Vinu Bharath R <vinubhar@qti.qualcomm.com>
